# The build context is the repo root rather than the worker directory, because `bench.py` is a
# sibling of `transcribe/`. This file is what keeps that from dragging the whole checkout in.
#
# It is deliberately not per-worker. While the repo held two workers each image carried the other's
# source — a few dozen KB of Python that nothing imports, against a base image of many GB — because
# excluding it would have meant one `.dockerignore` per image and a build that breaks the day a
# module moves. Same reasoning if a second worker lands again.
.git
.github
tests
corpus
bench-results.jsonl
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
*.md
